@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include ../rixte/shortfall/style.iuml

title Recipe deletion: selected classes and relationships
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 85
hide empty members

class MishMash {
  - {static} executeCommand(input: String, scanner: Scanner, ...): void
  - {static} userConfirms(scanner: Scanner, question: String): boolean
}
class Parser {
  + parseCommand(input: String): Command
  - parseDeleteRecipe(arguments: String): Command
}
interface Command {
  + confirmationPrompt(recipeBook: RecipeBook): Optional<String>
  + execute(recipeBook: RecipeBook): String
}
class DeleteRecipeCommand {
  - index: int
  + confirmationPrompt(recipeBook: RecipeBook): Optional<String>
  + execute(recipeBook: RecipeBook): String
  - findTarget(recipeBook: RecipeBook): Recipe
}
class RecipeBook {
  + size(): int
  + getRecipes(): List<Recipe>
  + remove(index: int): Recipe
}
class Recipe {
  - name: String
  + getName(): String
}

MishMash ..> Parser : asks for a Command
MishMash ..> Command : asks, then executes
Parser ..> DeleteRecipeCommand : creates
DeleteRecipeCommand .up.|> Command
DeleteRecipeCommand ..> RecipeBook : execution parameter
RecipeBook --> "0..*" Recipe : -recipes\n{ordered, nonunique}

legend bottom
  Only feature-relevant members are shown; constructors and most getters are omitted.
  Command.confirmationPrompt is a default method that returns an empty Optional; DeleteRecipeCommand overrides it.
  MishMash owns all console input and output, so DeleteRecipeCommand never reads the user's answer itself.
  index is the one-based number the user typed; RecipeBook.remove takes a zero-based index.
  Dashed arrows show dependencies or interface realization; solid arrows show stored references.
endlegend
@enduml
